  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+bx+1=4{x}^{2}+9x+1\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $b.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $9.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nb=9.\n$$",
